// llama.cpp spends RMS_NORM_MUL(256,24,T) + RMS_NORM_MUL(256,2,T) + two ROPEs
// + the CPYs into the cache on the same thing, five lines of its graph. Here
// they are one, because all three tensors are column ranges of the same fused
// projection (llm_attn_qkv, the plain arm of llm_gemm.comp) and all three end
// in the same layout — so the grid is simply "one (token tile, plane)" and the
// plane index says which of the three this workgroup is.
//
//	plane < heads                   query head p        norm, rope, scale
//	plane < heads + kvHeads         key head p-heads    norm, rope
//	plane < heads + 2*kvHeads       value head          neither
//	the one after that              the indexer's raw key, copied
//
// **The key and the value go into the cache, the query does not** (L7a). A
// query plane is `plane` padded token rows of this batch and is read once by
// the kernel behind this one; a key plane is the layer's own nKV cells and
// outlives the batch. So the store below scatters by *cell* — token t of the
// run is cell SEQ_PAST + t — and a batch boundary is allowed to fall in the
// middle of a 16-row fragment tile, which is why it is an element scatter and
// not a tile copy. The rotary follows the same position: SEQ_PAST + t, not t.
//
// The last plane is the one thing here that is not a head at all. The
// indexer's key is pooled `ratio` cells at a time and at decode those cells
// arrive in `ratio` separate batches, so the raw key needs a cache of its own
// — 128 halves a cell against the key's 512 — and this is the pass that has
// its fp32 row already addressed. It is a plane of this kernel rather than a
// dispatch of its own because llm_attn_idx.comp *reads* it, and two dispatches
// are how that ordering is guaranteed.
//
// The query's *gate* is the other half of each of its heads and is not touched
// here at all: it is consumed by the attention kernel's epilogue straight out
        barrier();
    }

    // Out. The query is a whole tile of this batch's plane and consecutive
    // lanes write consecutive halves of it. The key and the value are cells of
    // the layer's cache, and `past` need not be a multiple of the tile, so
    // each element is placed by its own cell — sixteen-wide runs rather than
    // one 512-byte one, which for the two kv heads is not where this kernel's
    // time is.
    uint base = outOff + (head * (pc.plane / TILE) + tt) * (HDT * TILE * TILE);
    uint cellTiles = pc.nKV / TILE;
    for (uint o = tid; o < HDT * TILE * TILE; o += WG) {
        uint c = o / (TILE * TILE);
        uint rem = o % (TILE * TILE);
        uint m, d;
        if (mode == 0u) {
            m = rem / TILE;              // (token, component)
            d = c * TILE + rem % TILE;
        } else {
            m = rem % TILE;              // transposed: (component, token)
            d = c * TILE + rem / TILE;
        }
        float v = rows[m * HEAD_DIM + d] * scale;
        if (!cached) {
            hact[base + o] = float16_t(v);
            continue;
